  "caveats": [
    "Clean-FFS-visible slice of the T-MSIS-derived file (~21% of program dollars; reconciles 18-25% of CMS-64 yearly).",
    "Managed-care encounter completeness varies by service type.",
    "Cells under 12 claims are suppressed at the source.",
    "2024 is claims-runout-truncated (December ~27% of run-rate).",
    "Z9525 (CA personal care) carries no provider NPI; it appears only in crossover_bases (plus_ca) and hcbs_code_yearbook.",
    "A claim line is not a 15-minute unit; median_paid_per_line is a rate-per-line series.",
    "State attribution is inverse-weighted across a provider's enrolled states; per-state visibility in state_provenance.",
    "Provider geography (zip5/county/rurality/svi) is the NPPES PRACTICE ADDRESS \u2014 it maps the caregiving industry's locations, never care delivery; multi-state organizations concentrate at HQ (check attributed_states).",
    "state_code_year suppresses cells built from <25 rows; median_paid_per_line is a rate over enrolled-provider rows, not an inverse-weighted total.",
    "who_* tables group billing NPIs into organizations via the entity layer: uniform rules (government keys + calibrated heuristics) plus a hand-verified curated overlay with per-row provenance; families as-of 2026-06; rankings depend on grouping and the exhibit states so.",
    "who_race_monthly.gap_flag marks entity-months below 20% of the entity's own median month \u2014 state submission gaps (e.g. one agency loses most billing NPIs for exactly one state fiscal year), never program events. trailing12_M spans containing gap months are unreliable; runout_flag marks 2024-11/12 claims-runout truncation."
  ]
